{"abstract":"We show that, for every fixed positive integers $r$ and $k$, \\textsc{Max-Weight List $r$-Colorable Induced Subgraph} admits a polynomial-time algorithm on $kP_3$-free graphs. This problem is a common generalization of \\textsc{Max-Weight Independent Set}, \\textsc{Odd Cycle Transversal} and \\textsc{List $r$-Coloring}, among others. Our result has several consequences. First, it implies that, for every fixed $r \\geq 5$, assuming $\\mathsf{P}\\neq \\mathsf{NP}$, \\textsc{Max-Weight List $r$-Colorable Induced Subgraph} is polynomial-time solvable on $H$-free graphs if and only if $H$ is an induced subgraph of either $kP_3$ or $P_5+kP_1$, for some $k \\geq 1$. Second, it makes considerable progress toward a complexity dichotomy for \\textsc{Odd Cycle Transversal} on $H$-free graphs, allowing to answer a question of Agrawal, Lima, Lokshtanov, Rz{\\k{a}}{\\.z}ewski, Saurabh, and Sharma [TALG 2024]. Third, it gives a short and self-contained proof of the known result of Chudnovsky, Hajebi, and Spirkl [Combinatorica 2024] that \\textsc{List $r$-Coloring} on $kP_3$-free graphs is polynomial-time solvable for every fixed $r$ and $k$. We also consider two natural distance-$d$ generalizations of \\textsc{Max-Weight Independent Set} and \\textsc{List $r$-Coloring} and provide polynomial-time algorithms on $kP_3$-free graphs for every fixed integers $r$, $k$, and $d \\geq 6$.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Galby, Esther","Thomé de Lima, Paloma","Munaro, Andrea","Nikabadi, Amir"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828175"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Italy","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chalmers University of Technology","University of Parma"],"keyword":["cs DS","math CO"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"le